{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Zara's bicycle tire has a circumference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />m. If Zara travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />m on her bike, how many full rotations will her tire make?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c127a9d0bb5248b4cc60f202ed5dc45e38d1ffa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 900 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1350 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 600 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 450 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"460\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first break down what the problem is asking for. Since the circumference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> m, each full rotation will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> m. \n</p><p>Thus, we can divide the distance that Zara travels on her bike by the meters in each full rotation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0fe2c2ca667b7d66237e00b607f7d63d13d447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900 \\div 1.5 = 900 \\div \\frac{3}{2} = 900 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"346\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=